{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"68ffa0a7-2dae-408a-8305-ecaddde1f06a","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python/R. macOS primary since 2026-08-05; Windows 11 still active. Tool paths: CLAUDE.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads\\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE. 5 active, cap 5 (Fall). →Tier A prioritization-slate.\\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: NEXT: phone check; host or local? →Tier A personal-site-build-routes.\\n- **RTP CLA (9/10)**: NEXT: .ris → Zotero; lesson 0002. →Tier A rtp-cla.\\n- **ATH Tech**: shipped; ITS pending; run 9/29. →Tier A tech-inventory-refresh.\\n- **Status report**: #3 by 9/25, biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline.\\n- **GPS pull (9/21)**: Mac owns, 10:00+16:30. Win writer stopped (Eric, 9/22). No 16:28 wake. →`DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/`\\n- **VALD+Perch (9/21)**: Mac owns. Perch 10:05+16:35; VALD 10:10+16:40. Windows jobs off. →`_INBOX/docs/`\\n- **FB matchups (9/13)**: EPA = PFF; CFBD PPA cross-check. TRAP: `run_direction` != point of attack.\\n- **PP Recruiting (9/16)**: 010 + 011 matrix on Drive, pushed. NEXT: Eric reviews 011. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\n- **Sleep scheduler (9/16)**: R1 MERGED. NEXT: night/early-kickoff itineraries. →`sleep-scheduler/docs/`\\n- **RI5 #002 (9/21)**: VERIFIED + v2 PUBLISHED to Drive (28/30 ok, 2 read OK; 7 cites + \\\"case series\\\" fixed). NEXT: Eric sends `_v2` only.\\n- **TypeSafe (9/21)**: router LIVE both boxes (Mac 149/149); verifier LIVE, reads printed pages. 7 measured off map (surgery notes last). NEXT: Eric Y/Ns 22 surgeries, 12-mo rule (PR #21). Rec: maintenance; #3 = Eric's call. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- Hooks: patch both copies only for shared events; Codex has no prompt-submit event. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries copy nothing alone; sweep nested `~/.claude` repos and flag non-main branches. →handoff 2026-09-19-backup-divergence-fix.md\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` is a private I-983 repo. Keep private. Folder has a space; repo an underscore.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture (Mon, 8/24–1/23) →cfb-forecast-capture. Portfolio dashboard →command-centre.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- **OKR gate scored 9/14; still undecided**: AI integration buy-in + data governance (Anthony's proposal). Fold into NCAA charter or parking lot?\\n- **Kitman vs MyLink**: MyLink (~half Kitman cost) + Kitman API access. Undecided; blocks priority 3.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n[2026-09-21T23:30:11.684558+00:00] compiler-backlog: 2 log(s) backlogged, compiling newest 2 this run - run compile.py manually to catch up\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4271 chars, updated 2026-09-22 12:15)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":458},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fbd3e2ad-abad-40fd-ba2d-d7eae552f00d","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:25:24.794Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
