{"parentUuid":"bf952e0d-7ac8-4192-b9c8-cfd5ec45de24","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e21bdef7-ccb4-405a-9b5b-c5238bd3f038","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:25:26.854Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e21bdef7-ccb4-405a-9b5b-c5238bd3f038","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"UserPromptSubmit","toolUseID":"f850d24f-6296-494d-b402-3ae574fcabc5","hookEvent":"UserPromptSubmit","content":"<skill_relevance>\nNo skill in the roster appears relevant to this request.\n</skill_relevance>","stdout":"<skill_relevance>\nNo skill in the roster appears relevant to this request.\n</skill_relevance>\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"python3 \"$HOME/.claude/skill-router/router.py\"","durationMs":828},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4e7ffcdd-64b0-4e9e-b133-ea3bc51fcc1d","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:25:27.690Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nUserPromptSubmit hook success: <skill_relevance>\nNo skill in the roster appears relevant to this request.\n</skill_relevance>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
{"type":"atis-latch","atis":"","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb"}
{"parentUuid":"4e7ffcdd-64b0-4e9e-b133-ea3bc51fcc1d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/CLAUDE.md","type":"User","content":"# Machine\n\nMachine-specific shell, paths, and traps live in `~/.claude/machine.md` (gitignored; copy `machine.macos.md` or `machine.windows.md` to `machine.md` on a new machine). It is imported below.\n\n@machine.md\n\nTwo machines share this setup: the MacBook (`~/DEV`) and the Baylor Windows laptop (`~/Desktop/DEV`). Projects sync through GitHub (`erash11`), documents through Google Drive. Every project repo carries a Session routine in its `AGENTS.md`: `git pull` + read `docs/STATUS.md` at start; update `STATUS.md`, commit, `git push` at end.\n# Workflow Expectations\n\n- When asked to **create, merge, or consolidate an artifact** (calendar, deck, doc), the expected deliverable is always a produced file. Verify what exists first, then create the artifact regardless — never conclude with \"it already exists\" instead of delivering the file.\n- When the user types `/graphify`, invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` before doing anything else.\n\n# Session Startup\n\nHandled by the `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook — do not read these files by hand. It injects `global-memory/USER.md`, `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, `transcripts/.errors.log` (only when non-empty), and a pointer to the KeystoneOS snapshot.\n\n- If `.errors.log` content appears, surface it once on the first response, then continue. It is normally empty; entries mean hook failures.\n- If a **\"SessionStart hook could not read a required memory file\"** block appears, say so on the first response instead of working around it.\n- **If no `## User profile` block is in context at session start, the hook did not fire.** Say so, then read `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` and `transcripts/.errors.log` by hand.\n- What the hook injects is a frozen snapshot. Mid-session writes take effect next session. Never load more than this proactively.\n\n# Memory — routing only\n\nThe two-tier memory system (`~/.claude/global-memory/` and `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`) is owned by the **`memory-write` skill**, which holds the tier rules, character caps, slug rules, write steps, retrieval ladder, and daily-compiled-log rules.\n\nThe active project's Tier A memory (`~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`, indexed by its `MEMORY.md`) is **auto-injected by the harness** each session. Tier A files are also indexed by memsearch, so they stay recallable across projects.\n\n- Writing a fact — \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"save this\", \"forget about\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`\n- Recalling past context — \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about X\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`, retrieval-ladder section\n- Daily compiled logs at `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/daily/` are owned by `claude-memory-compiler`. Never hand-edit them; never read them eagerly.\n- **Slugs differ per machine** (Mac `-Users-kristinarash-DEV-<X>`, Windows `C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV-<X>`). Tier A written on one is not auto-injected on the other; memsearch still finds it. Durable project facts belong in the repo's `docs/` so both machines see them.\n\nDo not restate the memory procedure in this file. It has one home, and that home is the skill.\n\n---\n\n`AGENTS.md` is the sibling of this file for harnesses that have no Skill tool (Codex and similar). It intentionally carries the memory rules as plain prose instead of routing to a skill. **The two files are not meant to be identical — do not \"fix\" the difference by symlinking them.**"},{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/machine.md","type":"User","content":"# Shell / Environment (macOS)\n\n- zsh/bash is the native surface on this machine. PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`, `/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) is installed only to run the KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs natively.\n- **The tool-path list has one home: `~/.claude/TOOLPATHS.md`.** Read that file when you need a path. Only the traps below are kept, because acting on them wrongly is expensive.\n- **Verify, don't trust any list.** `which -a <tool>` is authoritative. To read PATH honestly, scrub the environment first:\n  `env -i HOME=\"$HOME\" USER=\"$USER\" TERM=xterm SHELL=/bin/zsh /bin/zsh -lic 'echo $PATH'`\n- Traps:\n  - Python is PEP 668-managed. Use venvs or `uv`, never `pip install` globally.\n  - `uv` is a standalone install at `~/.local/bin/uv`, **not** Homebrew. Claude Code hooks call `$HOME/.local/bin/uv`; do not delete or relocate it.\n  - `timeout` is NOT installed (no GNU coreutils). Don't use it in scripts.\n  - Homebrew owns `/opt/homebrew/bin`. `/usr/local/bin` is empty and stays that way.\n  - Secrets live in the macOS Keychain, not in `~/.zshrc`.\n- DEV projects live at `~/DEV` (not `~/Desktop/DEV`). Workspace map: `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`.\n- Primary storage drive (documents, data, deliverables): `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive`."}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ba6c8273-fda0-4d74-94cf-c34c8a0049f1","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:25:27.867Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/.claude/CLAUDE.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# Machine\n\nMachine-specific shell, paths, and traps live in `~/.claude/machine.md` (gitignored; copy `machine.macos.md` or `machine.windows.md` to `machine.md` on a new machine). It is imported below.\n\n@machine.md\n\nTwo machines share this setup: the MacBook (`~/DEV`) and the Baylor Windows laptop (`~/Desktop/DEV`). Projects sync through GitHub (`erash11`), documents through Google Drive. Every project repo carries a Session routine in its `AGENTS.md`: `git pull` + read `docs/STATUS.md` at start; update `STATUS.md`, commit, `git push` at end.\n# Workflow Expectations\n\n- When asked to **create, merge, or consolidate an artifact** (calendar, deck, doc), the expected deliverable is always a produced file. Verify what exists first, then create the artifact regardless — never conclude with \"it already exists\" instead of delivering the file.\n- When the user types `/graphify`, invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` before doing anything else.\n\n# Session Startup\n\nHandled by the `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook — do not read these files by hand. It injects `global-memory/USER.md`, `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, `transcripts/.errors.log` (only when non-empty), and a pointer to the KeystoneOS snapshot.\n\n- If `.errors.log` content appears, surface it once on the first response, then continue. It is normally empty; entries mean hook failures.\n- If a **\"SessionStart hook could not read a required memory file\"** block appears, say so on the first response instead of working around it.\n- **If no `## User profile` block is in context at session start, the hook did not fire.** Say so, then read `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` and `transcripts/.errors.log` by hand.\n- What the hook injects is a frozen snapshot. Mid-session writes take effect next session. Never load more than this proactively.\n\n# Memory — routing only\n\nThe two-tier memory system (`~/.claude/global-memory/` and `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`) is owned by the **`memory-write` skill**, which holds the tier rules, character caps, slug rules, write steps, retrieval ladder, and daily-compiled-log rules.\n\nThe active project's Tier A memory (`~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`, indexed by its `MEMORY.md`) is **auto-injected by the harness** each session. Tier A files are also indexed by memsearch, so they stay recallable across projects.\n\n- Writing a fact — \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"save this\", \"forget about\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`\n- Recalling past context — \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about X\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`, retrieval-ladder section\n- Daily compiled logs at `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/daily/` are owned by `claude-memory-compiler`. Never hand-edit them; never read them eagerly.\n- **Slugs differ per machine** (Mac `-Users-kristinarash-DEV-<X>`, Windows `C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV-<X>`). Tier A written on one is not auto-injected on the other; memsearch still finds it. Durable project facts belong in the repo's `docs/` so both machines see them.\n\nDo not restate the memory procedure in this file. It has one home, and that home is the skill.\n\n---\n\n`AGENTS.md` is the sibling of this file for harnesses that have no Skill tool (Codex and similar). It intentionally carries the memory rules as plain prose instead of routing to a skill. **The two files are not meant to be identical — do not \"fix\" the difference by symlinking them.**\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/.claude/machine.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# Shell / Environment (macOS)\n\n- zsh/bash is the native surface on this machine. PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`, `/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) is installed only to run the KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs natively.\n- **The tool-path list has one home: `~/.claude/TOOLPATHS.md`.** Read that file when you need a path. Only the traps below are kept, because acting on them wrongly is expensive.\n- **Verify, don't trust any list.** `which -a <tool>` is authoritative. To read PATH honestly, scrub the environment first:\n  `env -i HOME=\"$HOME\" USER=\"$USER\" TERM=xterm SHELL=/bin/zsh /bin/zsh -lic 'echo $PATH'`\n- Traps:\n  - Python is PEP 668-managed. Use venvs or `uv`, never `pip install` globally.\n  - `uv` is a standalone install at `~/.local/bin/uv`, **not** Homebrew. Claude Code hooks call `$HOME/.local/bin/uv`; do not delete or relocate it.\n  - `timeout` is NOT installed (no GNU coreutils). Don't use it in scripts.\n  - Homebrew owns `/opt/homebrew/bin`. `/usr/local/bin` is empty and stays that way.\n  - Secrets live in the macOS Keychain, not in `~/.zshrc`.\n- DEV projects live at `~/DEV` (not `~/Desktop/DEV`). Workspace map: `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`.\n- Primary storage drive (documents, data, deliverables): `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive`.\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ba6c8273-fda0-4d74-94cf-c34c8a0049f1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"session_context","context":{"userEmail":"The user's email address is eric.rash11@gmail.com. Use it only to identify the user, such as for authorship, attribution, or filtering their own work. Never send it to an unrelated service, such as in a request header, URL, or payload, unless the user explicitly asks."}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0a8752db-544b-4ae7-b2e4-39678da7d4fd","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:25:27.867Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# userEmail\nThe user's email address is eric.rash11@gmail.com. Use it only to identify the user, such as for authorship, attribution, or filtering their own work. Never send it to an unrelated service, such as in a request header, URL, or payload, unless the user explicitly asks.\n\nIMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0a8752db-544b-4ae7-b2e4-39678da7d4fd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"date","date":"2026-09-22"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f89f47c2-a273-4198-a089-a1a27f86fbd9","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:25:27.867Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nToday's date is 2026-09-22.\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
{"type":"last-prompt","leafUuid":"f89f47c2-a273-4198-a089-a1a27f86fbd9","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb"}
{"type":"atis-latch","atis":"","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb"}
{"parentUuid":"f89f47c2-a273-4198-a089-a1a27f86fbd9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKGCjWcSbhCgiWmiEYuy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Context:** Ran `/dev-sync` to bring the Mac in line with GitHub, decided two open GPS items, then ran `/closeout` for 2026-09-22.\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- Open decision on the 16:28 Mac wake for Perch/VALD pulls → Eric chose Option 2 (leave it). He also confirmed the Windows GPS job is stopped.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- **No `pmset` wake.** Perch and VALD may land up to 1 hour late when the Mac sleeps. Undo/enable command kept in `DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md`: `sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRFSU 16:28:00`.\n- Windows GPS writer marked stopped (per Eric's report; not verifiable from the Mac). Two writers = two mismatched databases.\n- Did **not** run `compile.py` — a run costs ~$1.28, so it is Eric's call, not an auto-action.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- Transcript log conflicts between Mac and Windows resolve cleanly with **union merge** — keeps every line from both machines, no `.from-*` files to clean up.\n- A **folder name with a space** (`DEV/Linda Projects`) broke one sync step; had to redo it quoted.\n- The backup manifest does not auto-discover new repos. `TOS_Evidence_Brief` was missing, which made the 09:05 backup report an error. Adding it to `~/.claude/scripts/backup-manifest.json` fixed it.\n- Tier A memory does not cross machines — durable GPS decisions were written into the repo's `docs/STATUS.md` plus `global-memory/MEMORY.md` so Windows sees them.\n\n**Sync results (146 repos walked):**\n- Pulled: `_INBOX` (1), `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` (2). Pushed: `CommandCentre` (`server.out`). Cloned: `TOS_Evidence_Brief` (made on Windows 9/21). 22 active, 117 dormant and clean. No conflicts.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `~/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md`\n- `~/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md`, `transcripts/.errors.log`, `transcripts/2026-09-21.md`, `transcripts/2026-09-22.md`\n- `~/.claude/scripts/backup-manifest.json` (backup at `backup-manifest.json.bak-2026-09-22`)\n- `~/DEV/TOS_Evidence_Brief/` (new clone), `graphify-out` (13 files from nightly job)\n\n**Action Items:**\n- **Open:** memory compiler still has 2 backlogged logs; warning stays in `.errors.log` until Eric runs `compile.py` (~$1.28). Command is in `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/README.md`.\n- Revisit the wake decision only if GPS data goes **missing**, not merely late.\n- Carried over from earlier: test Perch/VALD failure alerts; delete `FA2026/_Mark_for_Deletion/gps_db_handoff_2026-09-21/` on Drive."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":43124,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1103,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":43124,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1103,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":43124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":43124},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfKGCj4aCDY66iT5VVTG2","type":"assistant","uuid":"737aec27-3c40-4aa2-8dcc-d401f502b70a","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:25:39.793Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"737aec27-3c40-4aa2-8dcc-d401f502b70a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__batch","description":"Create a doc, or apply several operations to one doc atomically.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"batch":{"type":"array"},"container":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string"},"id":{"type":"string"},"create":{"type":"object"}},"required":["kind"]},"verbose":{"type":"boolean"},"opId":{"type":"string"}}},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__guide","description":"Docs guides: topic.instructions repeats the server instructions. Read it only if your client dropped them. Also topic.<name>, refusal.<code>. After a doc's birth → [\"topic.index\"].","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"items":{"type":"array","description":"topic.<name> (instructions, index, editing, tabs, comments, charts, chart-definition, uploads, skill) or refusal.<code>; several per call is fine."}}},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__update","description":"Edit a tab's contents, rename a doc or tab, or change a stored value.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ref":{"type":"object","properties":{"object":{"type":"string","enum":["project","file","node","utterance","enum"]},"id":{"type":"string"}},"required":["object","id"]},"engine":{"type":"string"},"payload":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object"},{"type":"string"}]},"container":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string"},"id":{"type":"string"},"version":{"type":"string"}},"required":["kind","id"]},"verbose":{"type":"boolean"},"opId":{"type":"string"},"answering":{"type":"string","maxLength":64}},"required":["ref","payload"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"904d5f41-9234-487c-bef0-b4a21fc9ae96","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:25:39.975Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"1a64884c-3e4a-4736-8120-e44db2d3bffb","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
